### Phase 2 — Dead Code + SSOT Violations · 3 issues

**3. Dead computed properties — exact duplicates of existing properties**

`MainViewModel+Insights.swift`:

```swift
var hasBriefingAvailable: Bool { self.currentInsight != nil }   // L50 — identical to hasInsightAvailable (L28)
var hasUnreadBriefing: Bool { self.hasUnreadInsight }            // L51 — pure alias, never used in any view/component
```

`grep -rn "hasBriefingAvailable\|hasUnreadBriefing"` finds zero usages in `Views/` or `Components/`.
Both are dead. `hasBriefingAvailable` also violates SSOT: two properties returning `self.currentInsight != nil`.

**4. Gemini model name strings not centralized — SSOT violation in `functions/index.js`**

| Line | Value |
|---|---|
| 74, 170, 245 | `"gemini-2.5-flash-lite"` (raw string, three occurrences) |
| 444 | `"gemini-2.5-flash"` (different model, no comment explaining why) |

Two different model tiers are used across four call sites with no named constants and no explanation
for the tier difference. When the model is upgraded, all four lines must be found and edited by hand.

